1565 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Freelance UX Researcher\nSIT\n2023 \205 2024\nDeveloped corporate branding and visual identity solutions\054 establishing a cohesive brand visual language across digital and physical communication channels\056\nLed a multi\055phase UX research initiative supporting the redesign of the company\047s corporate website\054 navigation\054 and digital experience\056\nConducted surveys\054 focus groups\054 usability audits\054 and qualitative research to identify user needs\054 behavioral patterns\054 and business opportunities\056\nSynthesized research findings into actionable recommendations for navigation redesign\054 information architecture\054 and user\055centered digital experiences\056\nCollaborated with stakeholders to align product design decisions with brand consistency\054 business objectives\054 and customer expectations\056\n\nFreelance UX\057UI Designer\nSJO Turismo \057 Municipalidad de San Jos\351\n2020\0552022\nDesigned a mobile tourism product focused on cultural exploration\054 route planning\054 navigation\054 and accessible digital experiences\056\nDeveloped a scalable design system in Figma using Atomic Design principles\054 reusable component architecture\054 and standardized visual and interaction patterns\056\nCreated user flows\054 journey maps\054 wireframes\054 and high\055fidelity interactive prototypes to simplify complex navigation and route\055planning experiences\056\nConducted task\055based usability testing with 15 participants across three user personas\054 evaluating task completion\054 navigation efficiency\054 and interaction patterns\056\nIterated product designs based on qualitative and quantitative research findings\054 prioritizing usability\054 accessibility\054 and visual consistency\056\nCollaborated with multidisciplinary teams from TEC and local government stakeholders\054 supporting product discovery\054 requirements definition\054 and Agile product development\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 1566 0 R
     /Pg 1560 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

