1569 0 obj
  << /ActualText (OneDesk \174 Walmart Central America\nB2B SaaS \046 Enterprise UX \267 Complex Workflows \267 Design Systems\n\nDesigned a unified enterprise platform integrating three operational modules and role\055based experiences for five distinct user profiles\056\nApplied Walmart\047s Living Design System\054 leveraging reusable components\054 design tokens\054 official iconography\054 and standardized interaction patterns to ensure brand consistency and scalability\056\nDesigned advanced filtering\054 bulk actions\054 registration flows\054 approval workflows\054 and comprehensive interface states\056\nDeveloped functional HTML\057CSS\057JavaScript prototypes to support technical validation and engineering handoff\056\nSupported projected annual operational savings of \044434\054000 and a targeted 5\045 reduction in print volume\056\n\nEnterprise Analytics \046 Commercial Intelligence \174 Walmart Central America\nAnalytics Dashboard Design \267 B2B Onboarding \267 Merchandising \267 Advanced Figma\n\nDesigned commercial\054 sales\054 merchandising\054 and marketing dashboards supporting data\055driven business decisions\056\nDeveloped reporting interfaces for analyzing sales performance by product\054 category\054 and store\054 as well as digital marketing campaign performance\056\nDesigned B2B onboarding experiences through guided product walkthroughs\054 breadcrumb\055based onboarding patterns\054 contextual guidance\054 and user manuals\056\nLeveraged advanced Figma component architecture\054 variants\054 Auto Layout\054 shared libraries\054 and reusable data visualization components to ensure design consistency and scalability\056\n\nCecoApp \174 Cecotec \204 Master\047s Project\nAdvanced Figma \267 Component Architecture \267 Navigation Redesign \267 Digital Merchandising\n\nDesigned a mobile e\055commerce experience supported by a scalable Atomic Design system in Figma\054 including reusable components\054 variants\054 visual foundations\054 and page templates\056\nConducted open card sorting research with 31 participants\054 obtaining 16 complete responses across 45 content cards to inform navigation redesign and information architecture\056\nDesigned digital merchandising experiences through product discovery\054 category navigation\054 advanced filtering\054 product comparison\054 and personalized shopping journeys\056\nDeveloped high\055fidelity interactive prototypes\054 maintaining Cecotec\047s brand visual language and visual consistency throughout the experience\056\nValidated four core user journeys through task\055based usability testing and iterative design improvements\056\n\nE\055commerce Experience Analysis \174 Walmart Central America\nRetail UX Research \267 Digital Merchandising \267 Customer Experience\n\nEvaluated digital shopping journeys\054 product discovery\054 category navigation\054 promotional interactions\054 and checkout experiences\056\nAnalyzed usability barriers and customer behavior to identify opportunities for improving digital merchandising and purchase journeys\056\nTranslated qualitative and quantitative research findings into actionable product design and usability recommendations\056)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 1570 0 R
     /Pg 1560 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
