1603 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Senior Product Designer\nWalmart Central America\n2024\205Present\nDesign and evolve B2B\055style enterprise applications and data\055driven digital products supporting retail operations\054 commercial strategy\054 and business decision\055making across Central America\056\nLead analytics dashboard design across commercial\054 sales\054 merchandising\054 and marketing domains\054 transforming complex datasets and KPIs into actionable insights\056\nDesign reporting interfaces that enable stakeholders to analyze sales performance by product\054 category\054 and store\054 as well as monitor digital marketing campaign performance\056\nDesign B2B onboarding experiences for enterprise applications and analytics dashboards\054 implementing guided product walkthroughs\054 onboarding breadcrumb patterns\054 contextual guidance\054 and user manuals to facilitate product adoption and feature discovery\056\nSimplify complex enterprise workflows through navigation redesign\054 information architecture\054 role\055based experiences\054 advanced filtering\054 and progressive disclosure\056\nDemonstrate advanced Figma proficiency through scalable component architecture\054 reusable components\054 variants\054 Auto Layout\054 shared libraries\054 and high\055fidelity interactive prototypes\056\nApply and extend Walmart\047s Living Design System\054 ensuring brand visual language\054 component consistency\054 visual hierarchy\054 and technical scalability across enterprise products\056\nConduct UX research\054 stakeholder workshops\054 user interviews\054 and iterative usability testing to validate design decisions and identify product improvement opportunities\056\nCollaborate with Product Managers\054 software engineers\054 architects\054 data analysts\054 and business stakeholders throughout the product lifecycle\054 from discovery to implementation\056\nLeverage AI\055powered tools and functional prototyping to accelerate design exploration\054 technical validation\054 documentation\054 and developer handoff\056\n\nLead UX\057UI Designer\nGrupo Financiero CAFSA\n2022 \205 2024\nLed the UX\057UI redesign of corporate web platforms and mobile payment experiences\054 focusing on navigation redesign\054 information architecture\054 usability\054 and customer journey optimization\056\nLeveraged advanced Figma capabilities to develop user flows\054 wireframes\054 reusable components\054 variants\054 Auto Layout\054 and high\055fidelity interactive prototypes\056\nDeveloped a scalable design system with reusable component architecture\054 standardized interaction patterns\054 and visual guidelines to ensure consistency across digital products\056\nTranslated corporate brand visual language into cohesive digital experiences through typography\054 color systems\054 iconography\054 and visual hierarchy\056\nDesigned promotional campaigns\054 point\055of\055purchase materials\054 and merchandising\055related communication\054 ensuring brand consistency across physical and digital touchpoints\056\nConducted UX research\054 user interviews\054 journey mapping\054 and usability testing to identify friction points and validate design decisions\056\nCollaborated with business and technology stakeholders to translate complex financial requirements into intuitive\054 accessible\054 and scalable digital solutions\056)
     /K [ 11 ]
     /P 1604 0 R
     /Pg 1562 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

